NOT CONVERGED: 6 blocking issues at HEAD d5b2ab9 (wp/s3f, a clean tree). Two are new and proven by my own probes. The first is a correctness break: an owed re-route or a waiting join pinned to a job that a drained publication's ENOENT re-queued at the same epoch follows the later copy and gets that content's bytes, where visit-first answers notFound from the re-queued attempt's 404 (PROBE-C21C-PIN-ENOENT-404, 2/2 per case). This is the pin-caller sibling of 58b278e, and it falsifies ruling 6.3's 'equals the reference' for a terminal failure of the fresh attempt. The second is a C2 miss in the purge: withdrawPurged walks every job in one turn, 53.9 ms best at 10,000 jobs, 12.4 ms for one job of 10,000 ids, and 11.5-13.0 ms with 10,000 waiting joins, all at a 1-minute load under 8. Four more are the fixer's own open items, each reproduced or confirmed here:
